import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 669 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 670 | 2026-10-26 | **Grade 1 loose ends and Grade 3 floor marks (Build AF-0; the syllabus checks).** Built on row 669. (1) Chords drill, a tenth level 'Minor keys: i or V?' (Music Craft Grade 1: root-position I (i) and V in the grade's keys, harmonic minors A, E, D, G): the triad on the treble staff with the minor key's own signature, the key named above; V's middle note is the raised 7th, so it shows as an accidental; the answer says so. Before this the drill had major keys only. (2) Scales step 1 defines 'diatonic' (Music Craft Preliminary: 'understand the concept of diatonic'): belonging to the key, the seven notes of its scale; in C major the white keys are diatonic, the black keys are not. (3) Five Home lessons marked Grade 4 now carry the Grades 2-3 mark: 'Turn it upside down', 'The tritone' and 'Diminished and augmented' are Music Craft Grade 3 items (all diatonic intervals and their inversions; the augmented 4th and diminished 5th; diminished triads in root position and first inversion, augmented triads in root position); 'Question or answer phrase?' is Grade 3's cadences closing phrases and periods; 'Sequences' moves with it (its room, Melody & Phrasing, and its twin lesson are already on Grades 2-3). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch694.py. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
